WEBVTT

00:01.760 --> 00:03.950
The battle at the Kalos League Miare Tournament finals...

00:01.980 --> 00:11.820
While watching anime, make sure not to sit too close to the screen and that the room is well lit.

00:04.540 --> 00:11.620
...between Satoshi and Alan ended with a victory for Alan after a fierce fight between Gekkouga and Lizardon.

00:12.640 --> 00:16.930
However, in the middle of the closing ceremony, a strange incident occurred.

00:19.120 --> 00:20.040
The curtain rises...

00:20.580 --> 00:22.870
....for my greatest show!

00:45.520 --> 00:45.980
Manon is here?

00:46.440 --> 00:46.830
Yeah.

00:47.340 --> 00:48.750
She thought she'd get in the way during the finals,

00:49.280 --> 00:50.500
so she kept it a secret from you.

00:51.000 --> 00:51.550
Oh, that girl...

00:52.100 --> 00:52.900
She shouldn't have done that...

00:53.900 --> 00:54.310
But...

00:54.710 --> 00:56.300
...considering what happened, I thought I should tell you.

00:56.860 --> 00:57.900
She means a lot to you, doesn't she?

01:00.230 --> 01:00.480
Yeah.

01:01.330 --> 01:03.400
Let's go search for her. I'll help out as well.

01:09.740 --> 01:10.820
So this is happening outside too...

01:12.150 --> 01:12.810
Satoshi!

01:13.560 --> 01:14.100
Guys!

01:14.630 --> 01:15.600
Are you all right?

01:15.950 --> 01:17.140
Yeah, we're fine.

01:17.660 --> 01:20.670
Satoshi, Squishy ran off somewhere.

01:22.090 --> 01:27.350
The damages that started around the Prism Tower due to the outbreak of strange vines are still spreading.

01:27.720 --> 01:31.090
When evacuating, please make sure to move away from Prism Tower.

01:31.340 --> 01:32.050
I repeat.

01:32.440 --> 01:36.380
The damages that started around the Prism Tower due to the outbreak of strange vines are still spreading.

01:34.200 --> 01:35.370
What is that?

01:35.690 --> 01:36.380
It's glowing.

01:37.060 --> 01:37.580
Don't tell me that's...

01:38.200 --> 01:38.790
...Zygarde?

01:39.820 --> 01:40.620
Zygarde?

01:40.990 --> 01:42.880
Are these vines Zygarde's doing?

01:43.330 --> 01:43.850
No way...

01:48.250 --> 01:49.130
Respond!

01:49.730 --> 01:50.720
Respond!

02:17.840 --> 02:18.360
You...

02:18.800 --> 02:19.420
What is the matter with you?

02:20.520 --> 02:21.170
Answer!

02:21.970 --> 02:22.870
Answer!

02:29.230 --> 02:29.820
It's Squishy!

02:30.950 --> 02:32.840
Squishy is heading to the Prism Tower!

02:33.300 --> 02:34.360
What? Really?

02:34.700 --> 02:36.350
Yeah. Eureka knows!

02:36.350 --> 02:36.960
Eureka, wait!

02:37.720 --> 02:38.390
Citron, go!

02:38.800 --> 02:40.080
I'll catch up with you later, promise.

02:40.390 --> 02:40.950
What about you, Satoshi?

02:41.280 --> 02:43.410
I'll go look for Manon with Alan.

02:43.410 --> 02:44.040
But...

02:44.040 --> 02:45.390
We'll make sure to find her quickly and run after you.

02:45.390 --> 02:46.580
Wait, Satoshi...

02:47.520 --> 02:48.060
Take this!

02:49.370 --> 02:49.940
It is a communication device.

02:50.570 --> 02:53.300
I prepared these nice machines for times like this!

02:54.020 --> 02:56.640
Their waves are not very strong, but please use it if there is an emergency.

02:57.170 --> 02:57.610
Thank you!

02:58.070 --> 02:59.430
Be careful, Satoshi.

02:59.780 --> 03:00.080
Yeah.

03:01.460 --> 03:03.680
Please proceed this way and do not panic.

03:05.580 --> 03:07.400
Jukain, Leaf Blade!

03:13.620 --> 03:14.940
Now, hurry!

03:15.330 --> 03:16.590
We'll make a path!

03:17.240 --> 03:18.460
Come out, Fushigisou!

03:18.460 --> 03:19.800
Lizardon, please!

03:20.300 --> 03:21.210
Kamex!

03:26.080 --> 03:27.360
Everyone, this way!

03:33.330 --> 03:34.600
Green flames...

03:35.550 --> 03:36.940
...will wrap around Kalos...

03:37.490 --> 03:41.830
...and pull both humans and Pokémon into the vortex of its flames.

03:42.400 --> 03:45.440
Is this situation what Gojika-san had predicted?

03:47.530 --> 03:51.710
You will all play a major role in this vortex.

03:53.470 --> 03:54.810
Where are Satoshi-kun and the others...

03:55.370 --> 03:55.780
...right now?

04:01.340 --> 04:07.010
The Flare Gang Attacks!
The Zygarde at the Prism Tower!!

04:08.010 --> 04:17.860
Play a board game via the Pocket Monsters XY& data broadcast!
Press the d-button on your remote and try reaching the battles and the presents!!

04:08.010 --> 04:17.860
Z

04:17.270 --> 04:17.980
You aren't hurt, are you?

04:18.520 --> 04:18.780
No!

04:19.400 --> 04:20.400
Thank you very much!

04:20.990 --> 04:21.610
Junsa-san!

04:22.030 --> 04:23.860
How is the evacuation of the residents coming along?

04:24.280 --> 04:28.160
The entire police force is currently working on guiding the crowds, but the damage is spreading.

04:28.990 --> 04:29.830
I'm going there as well.

04:30.240 --> 04:30.790
Lead the way.

04:31.160 --> 04:31.330
Okay!

04:35.540 --> 04:37.380
Geez! What's going on?!

04:38.630 --> 04:40.510
It doesn't look like a natural outbreak.

04:40.510 --> 04:42.420
This is major! This is major!

04:43.130 --> 04:44.220
Fleur-de-lis...

04:44.220 --> 04:44.590
Huh?

04:48.180 --> 04:49.390
Manon!

04:50.220 --> 04:51.430
Manon!

04:52.560 --> 04:53.140
Alan!

04:53.730 --> 04:54.890
Alan!

04:56.270 --> 04:56.520
Manon!

04:57.400 --> 04:58.610
Manon, over here!

04:58.900 --> 05:00.190
Everyone's heading for the Prism To-

05:01.190 --> 05:01.780
Alan!

05:02.570 --> 05:03.360
We'll help you now!

05:04.070 --> 05:04.700
Lizardon!

05:08.620 --> 05:09.530
Dragon Claw!

05:15.210 --> 05:15.540
All right...

05:17.080 --> 05:18.580
Pikachu, Iron Tail!

05:26.090 --> 05:27.340
Using cars is dangerous!

05:30.140 --> 05:30.850
Answer!

05:31.560 --> 05:32.810
What happened to you?

05:34.390 --> 05:35.230
Hey!

05:35.230 --> 05:36.190
Where are you going?

05:36.850 --> 05:37.980
Our coverage is over.

05:38.480 --> 05:39.560
You guys can do as you please now.

05:39.770 --> 05:40.360
What?!

05:40.520 --> 05:41.520
Hey, wait!

05:41.820 --> 05:43.860
Don't we need to broadcast this incident?

05:44.900 --> 05:46.740
I remembered something important.

05:47.700 --> 05:48.660
Huh?

05:49.320 --> 05:50.370
What's up with her?

05:50.780 --> 05:51.580
All right, I've decided!

05:52.330 --> 05:53.830
I have an idea.

05:54.290 --> 05:54.580
Camera!

05:55.040 --> 05:55.330
Y...

05:56.000 --> 05:56.370
Yeah!

05:57.210 --> 05:58.040
Okay, go!

05:58.460 --> 05:59.420
Cue!

06:03.630 --> 06:04.710
Dear television viewers,

06:05.380 --> 06:07.220
we're at the Miare Stadium.

06:07.930 --> 06:12.430
Right now, the closing ceremony of the Kalos League is experiencing a strange incident.

06:13.260 --> 06:18.100
A group of plants that suddenly broke out is filling all of Miare City, beginning with the stadium.

06:19.020 --> 06:21.020
What is happening?

06:21.690 --> 06:26.110
I, Musamoto, will continue this emergency live broadcast at the risk of my life!

06:30.200 --> 06:30.660
How's that?!

06:34.330 --> 06:35.620
All right, attention, please!

06:37.750 --> 06:39.500
Will you listen to what I have to say?

06:40.170 --> 06:42.340
You're that woman who was after Squishy...!

06:42.540 --> 06:44.500
Oh my, you remember?

06:45.340 --> 06:47.340
But what we want to get today...

06:47.720 --> 06:48.800
...is you!

06:49.550 --> 06:49.970
Me?

06:51.550 --> 06:52.350
What do you mean?

06:53.010 --> 06:54.260
Director's orders.

06:55.430 --> 06:56.890
Do you know those people?

06:59.100 --> 07:00.020
Do you, Alan?

07:00.600 --> 07:01.690
He doesn't just "know" us,

07:02.150 --> 07:03.560
he's like a colleague!

07:04.190 --> 07:06.400
The people that were after Squishy, and Alan... they're...?

07:07.690 --> 07:08.860
What does this mean, Alan?

07:10.570 --> 07:11.450
Oh, right.

07:11.700 --> 07:14.490
Alan... One of my men is on his way to get her out of harm's way.

07:14.780 --> 07:16.200
You come with me.

07:16.660 --> 07:17.660
The director is calling for you.

07:18.450 --> 07:18.870
Alan!

07:19.330 --> 07:20.960
Don't believe what those guys are saying!

07:22.330 --> 07:22.630
Let's go!

07:25.960 --> 07:26.420
Alan...

07:28.840 --> 07:30.510
Dorapion, Confuse Ray!

07:39.310 --> 07:39.770
Alan...

07:40.060 --> 07:41.640
What on... earth is...

07:54.660 --> 07:58.160
Oh my, you love your Trainer, huh?

08:01.960 --> 08:02.540
Carry them.

08:03.040 --> 08:03.330
Roger!

08:11.260 --> 08:14.890
This is Musamoto, reporting from the Miare Stadium in real-time.

08:15.640 --> 08:18.810
As you can see, Miare City has suffered enormous damage.

08:19.020 --> 08:19.680
Huh?

08:20.180 --> 08:21.060
Something's off!

08:21.640 --> 08:21.930
What?

08:27.900 --> 08:30.900
Dear Kalos region, as well as the whole world:

08:31.690 --> 08:33.030
My name is Fleur-de-lis.

08:33.820 --> 08:37.320
The Flare Gang, which has formed under my will,

08:37.320 --> 08:38.030
That person is...!

08:38.200 --> 08:39.580
hereby declares:

08:40.870 --> 08:41.790
Fleur-de-lis-san?!

08:43.160 --> 08:44.790
We will rebuild this world...

08:45.370 --> 08:47.750
...into a more beautiful place.

08:50.920 --> 08:51.880
Pokémon Quiz.

08:52.420 --> 08:53.220
The answer is...?

08:55.050 --> 09:04.980
Coming up next:

08:55.050 --> 09:00.060
Rebuilding the world into a more beautiful place!?

08:55.970 --> 09:00.680
Pocket Monsters XY&Z is brought to you by these sponsors.

09:00.100 --> 09:04.980
What are the Flare Gang's ambitions?

09:11.650 --> 09:16.490
We, the Flare Gang, will rebuild this world into a more beautiful place.

09:17.780 --> 09:18.700
This Pokémon...

09:19.330 --> 09:20.410
...is called Zygarde.

09:21.450 --> 09:24.660
It is a legendary Pokémon that surveys order in Kalos.

09:26.500 --> 09:32.340
We have joined forces with the tutelary Zygarde as guardians of the order.

09:34.130 --> 09:38.550
Zygarde is angered by the actions of humanity and Pokémon.

09:39.800 --> 09:42.430
The order of this world is already disturbed.

09:43.140 --> 09:44.890
Humans are nothing but fools.

09:45.520 --> 09:47.350
When there is only one of something, they won't share it.

09:48.940 --> 09:50.480
When they can't share it, they'll fight over it.

09:51.150 --> 09:52.860
And when something is fought over, some must survive without it.

09:53.900 --> 09:54.650
The only way to create...

09:55.400 --> 09:56.450
...a world where people live in beauty,

09:57.070 --> 09:58.360
a world without conflict or theft,

09:59.030 --> 10:01.370
is to reduce the number of lives.

10:02.120 --> 10:03.450
Only the chosen ones...

10:04.080 --> 10:05.540
...will live to see tomorrow!

10:07.830 --> 10:08.710
We, the Flare Gang,

10:09.670 --> 10:11.340
together with Zygarde's rage,

10:11.790 --> 10:13.800
will carry out the punishment.

10:15.630 --> 10:18.130
As its order has been disturbed, we will reset this world...

10:18.630 --> 10:20.090
...and create...

10:20.340 --> 10:21.720
...a beautiful world.

10:27.730 --> 10:28.350
Why...?

10:29.310 --> 10:30.020
Manon-sama.

10:30.770 --> 10:33.190
Fleur-de-lis-sama has sent word that he wants you brought to him.

10:34.690 --> 10:36.320
You're bad guys too, aren't you?

10:37.030 --> 10:37.360
No.

10:38.240 --> 10:40.700
We're just doing this for the sake of peace.

10:41.370 --> 10:41.740
No...!

10:44.790 --> 10:45.410
Professor!

10:45.740 --> 10:48.790
Forcing a lady to do something she doesn't want to do...

10:49.170 --> 10:50.210
I can't say I care much for that.

10:50.540 --> 10:51.460
What are you doing?!

10:51.960 --> 10:52.500
You...!

10:55.090 --> 10:55.800
Scorpi,

10:56.170 --> 10:56.510
Poison Sting!

10:56.840 --> 10:57.340
Gablias,

10:57.720 --> 10:58.800
Dragon Claw!

11:24.740 --> 11:25.450
Are you all right?

11:26.290 --> 11:27.660
Yes. Thank you, Professor.

11:28.290 --> 11:29.330
But more importantly, Alan was...

11:29.790 --> 11:30.500
You've seen him?

11:31.120 --> 11:32.290
He was with Satoshi.

11:33.210 --> 11:34.840
He said something about the Prism Tower.

11:35.710 --> 11:36.380
I see.

11:37.090 --> 11:39.170
You see, Satoshi-kun and the others might be in danger.

11:39.720 --> 11:39.880
What?!

11:40.510 --> 11:41.720
Let's head to the Prism Tower.

11:42.260 --> 11:43.430
Don't leave my side.

11:44.010 --> 11:44.390
Okay.

11:45.300 --> 11:46.100
Also, Professor...

11:46.760 --> 11:48.810
Fleur-de-lis-san's broadcast earlier...

11:49.520 --> 11:49.770
Yeah.

11:50.430 --> 11:53.150
We have to be cautious and find out the truth.

12:03.660 --> 12:05.870
Oh, Alan! The director is waiting for you.

12:06.580 --> 12:07.450
What's with that Zygarde?

12:08.120 --> 12:08.870
And why did you capture Satoshi?

12:09.330 --> 12:11.870
The director will tell you the details.

12:27.050 --> 12:27.470
Director.

12:28.930 --> 12:29.810
There you are, Alan.

12:31.270 --> 12:31.930
What do you think?

12:32.270 --> 12:33.810
Don't you think this is wonderful?

12:35.400 --> 12:37.980
Thanks to you, the system is complete.

12:38.730 --> 12:39.360
No way...

12:39.900 --> 12:40.730
But I still...

12:41.490 --> 12:44.280
This is the peace I've been wishing for.

13:11.930 --> 13:12.810
Look.

13:13.640 --> 13:15.890
The unsightly are disappearing gradually.

13:16.560 --> 13:18.020
Isn't it beautiful?

13:19.230 --> 13:22.320
Zygarde is representing our anger.

13:22.990 --> 13:23.780
Destroying a city...

13:24.280 --> 13:25.110
...and hurting people...

13:25.700 --> 13:27.950
Is that what you call peace?

13:28.740 --> 13:29.740
You said you wanted to protect...

13:30.410 --> 13:30.780
Yeah.

13:31.620 --> 13:32.290
We will protect...

13:33.750 --> 13:35.250
...the chosen ones, and them only.

13:50.260 --> 13:51.260
What is wrong?

13:51.720 --> 13:53.600
Can you not hear us?

13:58.060 --> 13:58.770
Answer!

13:59.230 --> 14:00.770
Do you not recognize us?

14:02.570 --> 14:03.820
There you are, Z1.

14:12.990 --> 14:14.240
There is no end to them.

14:25.090 --> 14:26.800
Oh, Citroid!

14:27.300 --> 14:29.590
Citron-sama, I am sorry to keep you waiting.

14:30.800 --> 14:32.260
Thank you, Elezard!

14:32.720 --> 14:36.430
If my master is in trouble, I will come to him no matter where he is!

14:37.140 --> 14:38.520
I expected nothing less, Citroid.

14:39.230 --> 14:40.440
Please give us a hand.

14:40.980 --> 14:42.480
We want to go to the Prism Tower.

14:43.070 --> 14:43.820
Of course!

14:45.530 --> 14:45.900
Watch out!

14:51.620 --> 14:53.280
That was close, guys.

14:54.200 --> 14:54.330
Ha!

14:54.790 --> 14:55.950
Burshamo Mask!

14:58.580 --> 15:01.000
Now that I'm here, you can feel safe.

15:01.460 --> 15:05.550
Burshamo Mask, the source of the incident seems to be at the Prism Tower.

15:06.590 --> 15:09.220
If we do something about that, we can protect Miare City.

15:09.800 --> 15:10.180
I got it.

15:10.590 --> 15:11.760
In that case, I'll go.

15:12.510 --> 15:13.720
You guys should turn back.

15:14.300 --> 15:14.640
No way!

15:15.720 --> 15:17.810
My Gym is over there!

15:18.060 --> 15:18.390
And Squishy!

15:19.180 --> 15:19.810
It's dangerous!

15:20.730 --> 15:21.810
You have no idea what's gonna be there.

15:22.480 --> 15:23.900
You might die!

15:24.400 --> 15:25.070
Please!

15:25.440 --> 15:26.360
It's my precious friend.

15:26.900 --> 15:29.030
I do not want to surrender my Gym any more!

15:29.900 --> 15:32.070
That place is filled with precious memories!

15:34.030 --> 15:34.620
If I do not go,

15:35.120 --> 15:36.870
I will regret this my whole life.

15:37.240 --> 15:37.870
Please!

15:38.200 --> 15:39.330
Please!

15:41.790 --> 15:42.420
I got it.

15:43.080 --> 15:44.540
Follow behind me.

15:45.290 --> 15:48.130
But you have to promise me you'll run away immediately if things get dangerous.

15:48.800 --> 15:49.550
Okay!

15:52.010 --> 15:53.390
Wake up!

16:16.450 --> 16:16.950
Eureka?

16:17.450 --> 16:17.990
Squishy...

16:19.330 --> 16:20.040
What's wrong?

16:21.290 --> 16:22.580
Squishy is in pain.

16:23.500 --> 16:24.250
We have to hurry!

16:25.210 --> 16:26.290
Yeah, we're almost there.

16:29.380 --> 16:29.710
Director,

16:30.510 --> 16:31.470
you said...

16:32.300 --> 16:33.880
"If you want to protect something, become stronger."

16:34.680 --> 16:35.760
Is <i>this</i> what you meant?

16:37.300 --> 16:38.850
The strength to protect something, huh...?

16:40.140 --> 16:40.520
Alan...

16:41.270 --> 16:42.940
What are you really protecting?

16:43.560 --> 16:45.150
A tomorrow that will only end up being worse than today?

16:48.820 --> 16:50.570
Fleur-de-lis-sama, we're ready.

16:51.240 --> 16:51.780
Good.

17:10.550 --> 17:11.210
This is...

17:11.670 --> 17:12.550
...awful...

17:13.010 --> 17:13.800
Where's Squishy?

17:14.130 --> 17:15.550
Let's start by securing an entrance.

17:16.130 --> 17:17.140
Flamethrower!

17:20.310 --> 17:20.810
Burshamo!

17:21.600 --> 17:22.770
No mischief, okay!

17:23.230 --> 17:23.890
The Flare Gang!

17:24.890 --> 17:26.560
We won't let you go any farther.

17:27.310 --> 17:29.400
Authorized personnel only.

17:35.700 --> 17:37.660
Huh...? What's this?

17:41.660 --> 17:42.330
Gekkouga!

17:44.620 --> 17:45.160
Pikachu!

17:45.790 --> 17:46.580
Is everyone all right?

17:48.380 --> 17:49.710
Hey, Satoshi-kun.

17:50.840 --> 17:51.460
Fleur-de-lis-san!

17:52.000 --> 17:52.460
Alan!

17:53.010 --> 17:54.210
What is the meaning of this?

17:54.210 --> 17:55.380
Please let me go.

17:56.130 --> 17:58.340
I'm sorry for treating you roughly, but...

17:58.720 --> 17:59.760
...I can't do that.

18:01.890 --> 18:02.680
Zygarde?

18:04.430 --> 18:06.180
Alan, what does this mean?!

18:08.810 --> 18:09.560
Satoshi-kun...

18:10.190 --> 18:12.570
You might be one of the chosen humans.

18:15.400 --> 18:17.740
In that case, it is you guys who have to get out!

18:18.610 --> 18:20.370
The Miare Gym belongs to <i>me!</i>

18:20.820 --> 18:22.080
I am very much "authorized"!

18:22.580 --> 18:24.080
Oh my, he's splitting hairs.

18:24.080 --> 18:24.660
I know, right?

18:25.330 --> 18:27.500
So the Flare Gang has caused this incident, right?

18:28.000 --> 18:28.420
Yes.

18:29.000 --> 18:31.670
There seems to be no doubt they are doing something in there.

18:32.250 --> 18:35.420
The situation appears even worse than I thought.

18:37.010 --> 18:37.470
Squishy....

19:06.200 --> 19:06.830
Squishy!

19:07.660 --> 19:08.500
Z1?

19:31.900 --> 19:32.600
Squishy!

19:34.610 --> 19:35.400
Squishy is...

19:35.900 --> 19:36.650
...Zygarde?

19:40.740 --> 19:41.360
This can't be...

19:41.990 --> 19:43.490
I cannot believe it was actually Zygarde...

19:44.030 --> 19:45.120
Oh my...

19:45.490 --> 19:49.000
It looks like Fleur-de-lis-sama was able to lure it out as planned.

19:53.380 --> 19:56.000
If you do not listen to us, we will use force.

19:56.710 --> 19:58.210
You obstinate fool!

20:09.220 --> 20:13.520
As Miare City faces the danger of being destroyed, two Zygarde clash.

20:14.480 --> 20:16.360
What is the fate of Satoshi and his Pokémon, who have been taken prisoner?

20:16.980 --> 20:18.440
And what about Alan?

20:19.440 --> 20:21.780
Fleur-de-lis' ambitions run wild.

20:31.790 --> 20:32.410
Ladies and gentlemen,

20:32.790 --> 20:35.630
this time I will explain Zygarde,

20:36.170 --> 20:38.250
who is indispensable for Operation Z.

